# Build-time variables. Copy to .env (gitignored) for a local build, and set the
# same names as BUILD variables in Workers Builds.
#
# Build variables only. The two SECRETS this site needs — RESEND_API_KEY and
# TURNSTILE_SECRET — must be Worker secrets instead:
#
#     npx wrangler secret put TURNSTILE_SECRET
#
# A secret added under Build settings is visible while the build runs and absent
# when the route executes, so the form fails in production against a build that
# passed. That is the single most expensive mistake available here.

# The Turnstile sitekey. Public by design — it is readable in the page source —
# but not committed, so staging and production can carry different widgets.
#
# Create the widget at:
#   Cloudflare dash -> Turnstile -> Add widget
#     mode      Managed
#     hostnames rexdalemobilewash.ca
#               www.rexdalemobilewash.ca
#               staging.rexdalemobilewash.ca
#               rexdalemobilewash.ash-47a.workers.dev
#
# All four. A preview hostname left off the list is a form that fails only on the
# preview, which is exactly where it gets tested.
#
# Without this, `npm run build` FAILS at bin/check-forms.mjs on all 15 form pages.
# That is deliberate: a build with no sitekey must not produce a deployable site.
PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITEKEY=

# Cloudflare's own test keys, for a local build with no widget of your own.
# The sitekey below always passes; pair it with the always-passes test SECRET
# (1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA) in dist/server/.dev.vars. Never deploy
# with these — they accept any token from anyone.
#   PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITEKEY=1x00000000000000000000AA
